<title>SWEDEN: Avesta Sheffield 6 mo profit slump.</title>
<headline>Avesta Sheffield 6 mo profit slump.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/British steel group Avesta Sheffield posts results for six months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>				     (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit				 24 vs  2,294</p>
<p> Invoiced sales			    8,415 vs 11,290</p>
<p> Operating result after deprec    LOSS  11 vs  2,242 PROFIT</p>
<p> Depreciation				  247 vs    250</p>
<p> Associate interest			   12 vs     52</p>
<p> Operating profit before fin net	   1 vs  2,294</p>
<p> Financial items		     CREDIT 23 vs    nil</p>
<p> Tax						23 vs    725</p>
<p> Profit before minorities		    1 vs  1,569</p>
<p> Minorities			    CREDIT 11 vs     19 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net profit				     12 vs  1,550</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Avesta Sheffield AB.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll found analysts expected Avesta Sheffield to show a pre-tax profit of 169 million crowns for the first six months of the split financial year.</p>
<p>NOTE: Avesta changed its reporting period this year, posting a 15 month result in March but then moving to a 12 month period in line with parent company British Steel Plc.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
